From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Halo 3] Smooth first-person weapons, object facing and the
 camera

- First-person weapon and arms poses (TLS[0x2D8], two slots per local
  player) are rebuilt once per tick in camera space, outside the object
  array. They are now snapshotted, blended and restored with the same hooks
  as objects, which removes the 30 Hz stepping of weapon bob, sway, recoil
  and reload animations.
- Object forward/up (+0x60/+0x6C) are blended too: first-person vehicle
  seats rotate the camera by them.
- Each tick replaces the cameras' copy of the player facing with the
  quantized simulation value, so frames alternated between quantized and
  exact facing (a 30 Hz shimmer, worst when scoped). The exact facing is
  copied back after the ticks; the game does the same copy itself before
  the next tick.
- Restoring after a frame no longer overwrites values that something else
  changed since the blend (a respawn or a new unit); those are kept and the
  object or pose starts over.
